{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.BoostFactorNZNormalization","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.BoostFactorNZNormalization","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BoostFactorNZNormalization.boost_factor_sqrt_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BoostFactorNZNormalization.boost_factor_sqrt_two","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BoostFactorNZNormalization.lean#L78-L89","doc":"**The boost factor is `√2` (the conditional structural identity).** For every real\ndeformation magnitude `x`, enhancing the rapidity by `√2` in the NZ-POTENTIAL–normalized\nquadratic form reproduces the cusp-SHAPE–normalized form:\n    `κ_pot·(√2·x)² = κ_shape·x²`.\nEquivalently: IF the bar-odd leak carries `κ_shape` (the open sub-obstruction, NOT\nasserted here), THEN the effective boost is `Re u = √2·ln q₀`, i.e. `c = √2`, `A = 2` —\nwith no free parameter. Derived from `(√2)² = 2 = κ_shape/κ_pot`, not fitted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BoostFactorNZNormalization.shape_over_pot_eq_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BoostFactorNZNormalization.shape_over_pot_eq_two","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BoostFactorNZNormalization.lean#L71-L76","doc":"**The exact amplification factor `A_shape = κ_shape / κ_pot = 2`.** This is the clean\nstructural value of the boost enhancement `A`: an observable carrying the cusp-shape\nquadratic form rather than the NZ-potential one is amplified by exactly 2. Falsifiable:\nthe ratio could have been any real; it is exactly 2 (the NZ ½). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BoostFactorNZNormalization.cuspShape_eq_two_mul_pot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BoostFactorNZNormalization.cuspShape_eq_two_mul_pot","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BoostFactorNZNormalization.lean#L66-L69","doc":"**The Neumann–Zagier ½.** `κ_shape = 2·κ_pot` — the cusp shape is exactly twice the NZ\npotential coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BoostFactorNZNormalization.cuspShape_eq_sin_pi_div_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BoostFactorNZNormalization.cuspShape_eq_sin_pi_div_three","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BoostFactorNZNormalization.lean#L61-L64","doc":"**`κ_shape = sin(π/3)`** — the cusp shape is the standard trig value, tying `√3/2` to the\nhexagonal `ζ₃` geometry `e^{iπ/3}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BoostFactorNZNormalization.cuspPotential_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BoostFactorNZNormalization.cuspPotential_pos","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BoostFactorNZNormalization.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BoostFactorNZNormalization.cuspShape_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BoostFactorNZNormalization.cuspShape_pos","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BoostFactorNZNormalization.lean#L58-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BoostFactorNZNormalization.cuspPotential","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BoostFactorNZNormalization.cuspPotential","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BoostFactorNZNormalization.lean#L53-L56","doc":"The Neumann–Zagier complex-volume **potential** coefficient `κ_pot = √3/4 = ½·κ_shape`\n(the same constant as `QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.cuspModulus`). The `½` is the\nNZ potential normalization. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BoostFactorNZNormalization.cuspShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BoostFactorNZNormalization.cuspShape","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BoostFactorNZNormalization.lean#L48-L51","doc":"The figure-eight cusp **shape** imaginary part `κ_shape = √3/2 = sin(π/3) = Im(e^{iπ/3})`.\nThe raw quadratic-form coefficient of the cusp, BEFORE the Neumann–Zagier ½ potential\nnormalization. ","signatureChunk":0}]}